  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Fiesole</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Faesulae (modern Fiesole) was an Etruscan foundation called Viesul, Vi\u015bl, or Vipsul. The city was conquered by Romans in 283 B.C. Sulla would settle Roman veterans there. Citizens of the town supported the conspiracy of Catiline.",
